/-!
# Fully faithful restriction of finite étale covers of a punctured spectrum

In the local Lefschetz situation `(A, f)` of Tag 0BLF, with `X = Spec A`, `X₀ = Spec (A/fA)` and
`U`, `U₀` the two punctured spectra, this file proves that the restriction functor
`FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` is fully faithful under the hypotheses of each of Stacks 0BM6, Stacks 0EK5 and
Stacks 0BLJ, for an arbitrary Noetherian local ring `A`.

The proofs are the source's. Each replaces `A` by its `𝔪`-adic completion `Â`, which is
Stacks 0BLI in the form
`…LocalLefschetzSituation.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_isAdicCompleteCase`; the side
conditions pass to `Â` by Stacks 0ALZ for Stacks 0BM6 and by Stacks 0BFR and Stacks 0EHW for
Stacks 0EK5 (`…LocalLefschetzSituation.annihilated_completion` and
`…LocalLefschetzSituation.depthDim_completion`). Over the complete ring `Â` the completion functor
along `(f)𝒪_U` is fully faithful on the finite locally free objects by Stacks 0EKS, respectively
Stacks 0EKT, and Stacks 0EL8 turns that into full faithfulness of `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}`.

## Main results

* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completionFullyFaithfulOn`
  `FiniteLocallyFree` — full faithfulness of `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` from full faithfulness of
  completion along `(f)𝒪_U`.
* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_annihilated_of_henselian` —
  **Stacks 0BM6**.
* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_depth_add_dim` — the case of
  Stacks 0EK5 in which hypothesis (c)(ii) holds.
* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_dualizingComplex` —
  **Stacks 0EK5**, with hypothesis (c) the disjunction of (c)(i) and (c)(ii).
* `…LocalLefschetzSituation.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_three_le_depth_of_henselian`
  — **Stacks 0BLJ**.

## Implementation notes

"`A` has a dualizing complex" is spelled
`∃ ω : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A), Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex ω`, with
`Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex` the predicate of [Stacks, Tag 0A7B]; this is the spelling of the
existence clauses of [Stacks, Tag 0BFR] and of `…LocalLefschetzSituation.DepthDim`.

Branch (c)(i) of Stacks 0EK5 is stated in the vocabulary of
`…LocalLefschetzSituation.two_lt_depth_add_ringKrullDim_of_propertySkRing_away`, which derives
branch (c)(ii) from it: `(S₂)` for `A_f` is `PropertySkRing (Localization.Away f) 2`, and the
irreducible components of `X` not contained in `X₀` are the `V(𝔮)` for the minimal primes `𝔮` of
`A` with `f ∉ 𝔮`, of dimension `dim(A/𝔮)`.

The identification of `U` with the complement of the zero locus of `𝔪` is
`…LocalLefschetzSituation.UOpen_eq_complementZeroLocus`, and the kernel ideal sheaf of `U₀ ⟶ U`
is generated by the restriction of `f` (`…LocalLefschetzSituation.ker_U₀ToU`), which is what the
ideal sheaf `(f)𝒪_U` of Stacks 0EKS and Stacks 0EKT is. Since both the scheme and the ideal sheaf
move when the open does, the open is generalized in a private auxiliary statement so that the
identification can be substituted.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BM6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BM6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EK5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EK5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EL8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EL8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ALZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ALZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AVZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AVZ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory IsLocalRing
open Stacks.FundamentalGroup Stacks.RelativeSpec
open Stacks.LocalCohomology (complementZeroLocus localCohomologyModule)
open Stacks.Algebraization (CompletionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree
  complementPrincipalIdealSheaf enatToEInt krullDimToEInt
  completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree_of_isAdicComplete_of_annihilated
  completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree_of_isAdicComplete_of_depth)

attribute [local instance 2000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace LocalLefschetzSituation

/-- The restriction functor `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` is fully faithful as soon as completion along
`(f)𝒪_U` is fully faithful on the finite locally free coherent sheaves on an open `W` of `X` equal
to `U`. -/
private theorem fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completion_aux
    (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u})
    (W : (Spec (CommRingCat.of S.A)).Opens) (hW : W = S.UOpen)
    (hcompletion : CompletionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree (W : Scheme)
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span
        {((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of S.A)).inv ≫ W.ι.appTop).hom S.f}))) :
    Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange S.U₀ToU).FullyFaithful := by
  subst hW
  rw [← S.ker_U₀ToU] at hcompletion
  exact fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree
    S.U₀ToU hcompletion

/-- The restriction functor `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` of the local Lefschetz situation is fully
faithful as soon as completion along `(f)𝒪_U` is fully faithful on the finite locally free
coherent sheaves on `U`.

This is Stacks 0EL8 for the closed immersion `U₀ ⟶ U`, in the form
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_completionFullyFaithfulOn`
`FiniteLocallyFree`, whose only input is full faithfulness of completion. -/
public theorem fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree
    (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u})
    (hcompletion : CompletionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree
      (complementZeroLocus S.A (maximalIdeal S.A) : Scheme)
      (complementPrincipalIdealSheaf S.A (maximalIdeal S.A) S.f)) :
    Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange S.U₀ToU).FullyFaithful :=
  fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completion_aux S
    (complementZeroLocus S.A (maximalIdeal S.A)) S.UOpen_eq_complementZeroLocus.symm hcompletion

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0BM6].** In the local Lefschetz situation assume that `H¹_𝔪(A)` and `H²_𝔪(A)`
are annihilated by a power of `f` and that `A` is henselian, or more generally that the pair
`(A, (f))` is henselian. Then `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` is fully faithful.

The proof is the source's. Replacing `A` by its `𝔪`-adic completion reduces the statement to the
case of an `f`-adically complete `A`, which is Stacks 0BLI in the form
`fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_isAdicCompleteCase`; the henselian hypothesis `hS` is
what that reduction consumes, and the annihilation hypothesis passes to the completion by
Stacks 0ALZ, which is `annihilated_completion`. In the complete case completion along `(f)𝒪_U`
is fully faithful on the finite locally free sheaves by Stacks 0EKS,
`Stacks.Algebraization.completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree_of_isAdicComplete_of_`
`annihilated`, and
`fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree` concludes. -/
@[stacks 0BM6]
public theorem fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_annihilated_of_henselian
    (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u})
    (hS : HenselianLocalRing S.A ∨ HenselianPair S.A S.principalIdeal)
    (h1 : ∃ n, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule S.A (maximalIdeal S.A)
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal S.A)) (ModuleCat.of S.A S.A) 1,
      S.f ^ n • x = 0)
    (h2 : ∃ n, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule S.A (maximalIdeal S.A)
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal S.A)) (ModuleCat.of S.A S.A) 2,
      S.f ^ n • x = 0) :
    Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange S.U₀ToU).FullyFaithful := by
  refine fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_isAdicCompleteCase S hS Annihilated ⟨h1, h2⟩
    S.annihilated_completion fun T hTcomplete hT => ?_
  exact fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree T
    (completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree_of_isAdicComplete_of_annihilated
      T.A (maximalIdeal T.A) T.f T.f_mem_maximalIdeal hTcomplete hT.1 hT.2)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0EK5] in the case of hypothesis (c)(ii).** In the local Lefschetz situation
assume that `A` has a dualizing complex, that the pair `(A, (f))` is henselian, and that
`depth(A_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭) > 2` for every prime `𝔭 ⊂ A` with `f ∉ 𝔭`. Then `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` is
fully faithful.

The proof is the source's. Replacing `A` by its `𝔪`-adic completion reduces the statement to the
case of an `f`-adically complete `A`, which is Stacks 0BLI in the form
`fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_isAdicCompleteCase`; the henselian hypothesis `hS` is
what that reduction consumes, and the other two hypotheses pass to the completion by Stacks 0BFR
and Stacks 0EHW, which is `depthDim_completion`. In the complete case completion along `(f)𝒪_U`
is fully faithful on the finite locally free sheaves by Stacks 0EKT,
`Stacks.Algebraization.completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree_of_isAdicComplete_of_depth`:
its condition at a pair of primes `𝔭 ⊆ 𝔮` with `𝔮 ⊇ 𝔪` is the condition here at `𝔭`, since
localizing the local ring `A` at a prime containing `𝔪` changes nothing. Then
`fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree` concludes.
The tag in full, with hypothesis (c) the disjunction of its two branches, is
`fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_dualizingComplex`. -/
public theorem fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_depth_add_dim
    (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u})
    (hS : HenselianPair S.A S.principalIdeal)
    (hdual : ∃ omega : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} S.A), Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex omega)
    (hdepth : ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum S.A, S.f ∉ p.asIdeal →
      enatToEInt
          (Module.depth (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal)
            (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal))
            (LocalizedModule p.asIdeal.primeCompl S.A)) +
        krullDimToEInt (ringKrullDim (S.A ⧸ p.asIdeal)) > ((2 : ℤ) : EInt)) :
    Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange S.U₀ToU).FullyFaithful := by
  refine fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_isAdicCompleteCase S (Or.inr hS) DepthDim
    ⟨hdual, hdepth⟩ S.depthDim_completion fun T hTcomplete hT => ?_
  obtain ⟨hdualT, hdepthT⟩ := hT
  refine fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree T
    (completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree_of_isAdicComplete_of_depth
      T.A (maximalIdeal T.A) T.f T.f_mem_maximalIdeal hdualT hTcomplete ?_)
  intro p q hp hq _
  rw [ringKrullDim_quotient_localization_of_maximalIdeal_le T.A q hq p.asIdeal]
  exact hdepthT p hp

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0EK5].** In the local Lefschetz situation assume

* (a) `A` has a dualizing complex,
* (b) the pair `(A, (f))` is henselian,
* (c) one of the following is true:
  * (i) `A_f` is `(S₂)` and every irreducible component of `X` not contained in `X₀` has
    dimension `≥ 3`, or
  * (ii) for every prime `𝔭 ⊂ A` with `f ∉ 𝔭` we have `depth(A_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭) > 2`.

Then the restriction functor `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` is fully faithful.

Hypothesis (a) is `hdual`, (b) is `hS` and (c) is the disjunction `hc`. In branch (c)(i), `(S₂)`
for `A_f` is `PropertySkRing (Localization.Away S.f) 2`, and an irreducible component of `X` not
contained in `X₀` is `V(𝔮)` for a minimal prime `𝔮` of `A` with `f ∉ 𝔮`, of dimension
`dim(A/𝔮)`. In branch (c)(ii) the depth of `A_𝔭` is that of `A_𝔭` as a module over itself along
its maximal ideal, and the inequality is read in the extended integers.

The proof is the source's: branch (c)(i) implies branch (c)(ii), by
`two_lt_depth_add_ringKrullDim_of_propertySkRing_away` — `A` is universally catenary by
Stacks 0A80 because it has a dualizing complex — and under (c)(ii) the statement is
`fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_depth_add_dim`: reduction to the `𝔪`-adic completion by
Stacks 0BLI, then Stacks 0EKT and Stacks 0EL8. -/
@[stacks 0EK5]
public theorem fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_dualizingComplex
    (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u})
    (hdual : ∃ omega : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} S.A), Dualizing.IsDualizingComplex omega)
    (hS : HenselianPair S.A S.principalIdeal)
    (hc : (PropertySkRing (Localization.Away S.f) 2 ∧
        ∀ q : Ideal S.A, q ∈ minimalPrimes S.A → S.f ∉ q →
          (3 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim (S.A ⧸ q)) ∨
      ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum S.A, S.f ∉ p.asIdeal →
        enatToEInt
            (Module.depth (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal)
              (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal))
              (LocalizedModule p.asIdeal.primeCompl S.A)) +
          krullDimToEInt (ringKrullDim (S.A ⧸ p.asIdeal)) > ((2 : ℤ) : EInt)) :
    Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange S.U₀ToU).FullyFaithful := by
  refine S.fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_depth_add_dim hS hdual ?_
  rcases hc with ⟨hS₂, hcomponents⟩ | hdepth
  · obtain ⟨omega, homega⟩ := hdual
    exact S.two_lt_depth_add_ringKrullDim_of_propertySkRing_away omega homega hS₂ hcomponents
  · exact hdepth

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0BLJ].** In the local Lefschetz situation assume that `A` has depth at least
`3` and that the pair `(A, (f))` is henselian. Then `FÉt_U ⟶ FÉt_{U₀}` is fully faithful.

This is the source's proof: depth at least `3` forces `H¹_𝔪(A) = H²_𝔪(A) = 0` by
[Stacks, Tag 0AVZ], through `Stacks.LocalCohomology.isZero_localCohomology_of_lt_depth`, so the
annihilation hypothesis of Stacks 0BM6 holds with any exponent and
`fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_annihilated_of_henselian` applies. The henselian
hypothesis is the more general of the two forms the source offers — `(A, (f))` a henselian pair,
rather than `A` henselian. -/
@[stacks 0BLJ]
public theorem fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_three_le_depth_of_henselian
    (S : LocalLefschetzSituation.{u})
    (hS : HenselianPair S.A S.principalIdeal)
    (hdepth : 3 ≤ Module.depth S.A (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) :
    Nonempty (finiteEtaleBaseChange S.U₀ToU).FullyFaithful := by
  have h3 : ((3 : ℕ) : ℕ∞) ≤ Module.depth S.A (maximalIdeal S.A) S.A := by
    exact_mod_cast hdepth
  -- Below the depth, `H^i_𝔪(A)` is zero, so every power of `f` annihilates it.
  have hann : ∀ i : ℤ, i < (3 : ℕ) → ∃ n : ℕ, ∀ x : localCohomologyModule S.A (maximalIdeal S.A)
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal S.A)) (ModuleCat.of S.A S.A) i,
      S.f ^ n • x = 0 := by
    intro i hi
    have hzero : CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero (localCohomologyModule S.A (maximalIdeal S.A)
        (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal S.A)) (ModuleCat.of S.A S.A) i) :=
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.isZero_localCohomology_of_lt_depth.{u, u} (maximalIdeal S.A)
          (ModuleCat.of S.A S.A) (by simpa using (maximalIdeal.isMaximal S.A).ne_top) 3 h3 i
          hi).of_iso
        (Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyWithSupportInIsoLocalCohomologyModule S.A
          (maximalIdeal S.A) (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal S.A))
          (ModuleCat.of S.A S.A) i).symm
    have hsub := ModuleCat.subsingleton_of_isZero hzero
    exact ⟨0, fun _ => hsub.elim _ _⟩
  exact fullyFaithful_finiteEtaleRestriction_of_annihilated_of_henselian S (Or.inr hS)
    (hann 1 (by norm_num)) (hann 2 (by norm_num))

end LocalLefschetzSituation

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
